# Editorial Layout Redesign

The current full-screen "immersive" UI causes visual overlap between the 3D graph/vectors and the mathematical matrices/text. This plan moves to a structured **Split-Panel Editorial Layout**, separating the conceptual narrative from the geometric visualization.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Layout Shift**: I am moving the "Narration" and "Formulas" from floating overlays to a dedicated **Sidebar (40% width)** on the left. The **Manim Canvas** will occupy the remaining **60% width** on the right.
> 
> **Matrix Location**: Matrices will now be rendered in the **Sidebar** using clean HTML/KaTeX instead of inside the WebGL canvas. This ensures they are always legible and don't block the view of the vectors.

